====Usage notes====
* In formal usage, ''England'' referring to Great Britain or the United Kingdom is now very rare.
* In common speech, ''England'' continues to be the most common word for the two respective entities ''as a whole''. It is, however, now uncommon to use ''England'' when referring specifically to a place or incident in Scotland, Wales, or Northern Ireland. In such a case, the respective word would normally be used ({{m|de|Schottland}}, {{m|de|Wales}}, {{m|de|Nordirland}}).
* The usage including the Republic of Ireland, which is sometimes heard, is conspicuously nonstandard.

